00:31:17,830 --> 00:31:23,029
And because the kernel requires some privileges, we kind of pretend we have them.

311
00:31:23,029 --> 00:31:26,149
And in many cases, even the drivers are using abstractions.

312
00:31:26,149 --> 00:31:33,590
We can just implement those abstractions kind of over the slightly higher level abstractions that exist in user space.

313
00:31:33,600 --> 00:31:38,389
Yeah, I hadn't even considered being able to use hardware devices.

